WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.650
<i>War is always with us.</i>

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.910
<i>Even here in this day care.</i>

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.300
<i>The day care sandbox.</i>

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.490
<i>It's said you will learn
all of life's lessons here.</i>

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.090
<i>This is a record of</i>

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.020
<i>a battle in the sandbox.</i>

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.500
This is our new friend, 
Amago Tsunehisa-chan.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:25.300
Everybody be nice to her.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:29.000
Nice to meet you, everyone.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:43.270
<i>She is Amago Tsunehisa:</i>

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:49.020
<i>the child who will bring war 
and chaos to the day care.</i>

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.880
It's time for recess!

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.650
Are you okay?

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:34.230
I'm okay.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:36.140
It's dangerous to run.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.340
I like playing in the 
sandbox, too, but...

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.140
I'll be careful.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.200
Wait a second.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:46.630
<i>This is how they met.</i>

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:50.510
<i>They say that in this 
moment, Shimizu-kun felt</i>

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:54.110
<i>something that would make 
him swear his life to her.</i>

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.070
It's time for dance.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:03.060
Everyone pair up.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.700
Let's dance together!

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:11.710
Thank you for pairing 
with someone like me.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.710
Why are you so nice?

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:18.760
I once played in a big 
sandbox all alone.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.760
So I know it's lonely to be alone.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:25.390
And you have talent, I'm sure of it.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.650
What kind of talent do I have?

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:32.240
Talent for a king.
Or, the talent to help a king.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:35.310
Are you the king, then, Tsunehisa-sama?

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:36.980
Yup.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:38.980
Lunchtime.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:41.720
Let's eat.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:48.420
I simply couldn't, Tsunehisa-sama.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.340
Go on.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.770
It's so red and pretty. 
You can have it.

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:55.620
You're so kind to someone like me...

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:57.890
I've got another, don't worry about it.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:03:58.750
But...

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:02.170
Then in exchange, 
help me with my dream.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:05.010
What is your dream?

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:10.520
To make a big sandcastle in 
the sandbox is my dream.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:16.610
Tsunehisa-sama, please 
make the sandbox yours.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.860
You can do it!

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.650
<i>Tsunehisa was four at the time.</i>

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.800
<i>Historians would later come</i>

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.120
<i>to recognize this as the beginning of</i>

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.500
<i>the great war for the sandbox.</i>

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:35.470
<i>It is true, partially, 
that the amount of sand you have</i>

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:38.110
<i>is the greatest factor in 
control of the sandbox.</i>

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:42.510
<i>But Tsunehisa had focused 
on another aspect.</i>

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.720
Shimizu-kun, do you know 
what the first thing

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:48.250
we need to do to attain the sandbox is?

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:51.050
Go to where there's the most sand?

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:52.020
No.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.880
We want the place with the most water.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.400
Water?

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.080
You need water to harden sand.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:01.980
So we start near the water.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:21.800
Slide 
Mountain

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:21.800
Faucet 
River

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:06.570
<i>In this era, the sand was 
divided into three parts.</i>

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:21.800
<b>Enya</b>

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.630
<i>The Enya-kun group, 
with the greatest size,</i>

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:11.570
<i>had the most sand and number of people.</i>

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:21.800
<b>Misawa</b>

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:13.550
<i>The Misawa-chan group,</i>

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:16.750
<i>with many toys and many games to play.</i>

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:21.800
<b>Matsuda</b>

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.910
<i>And the Matsuda-kun group, 
near the faucet and</i>

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:21.800
<i>with access to the most water.</i>

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.030
<i>Tsunehisa planned to enter</i>

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:27.320
<i>this Romance of the Three 
Kingdoms all by herself.</i>

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:31.620
See how big it is?

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:35.880
Those aren't real mudballs.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.440
He's wasting water.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:42.340
Shimizu-kun, Tsunehisa will show 
you how to make a real mudball.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:43.940
Okay...

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.450
Matsuda-kun!

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:47.570
Mind if I make some mudballs with you?

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:51.830
Okay, but can you make 
one bigger than me?

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.860
I bet you can't.

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:56.660
<i>"You disgusting fools, 
so proud of your mudballs' size."</i>

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:59.310
<i>Tsunehisa choked back those words.</i>

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:03.920
<i>"They still don't know what 
a real mudball can be."</i>

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:11.600
It's so small!

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:12.760
Tiny!

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:13.980
So tiny.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:14.890
It's tiny.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:17.640
Tsunehisa-sama.

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:19.650
It's not done yet.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:22.150
You'll know on Monday.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:30.730
Round!

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:31.970
It's so round.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:33.990
It's still small, though.

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:43.000
Wow!

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.170
It's shining!

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:46.700
It's black and shiny!

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:51.180
<i>Tsunehisa's mudball 
stunned Matsuda-kun's group.</i>

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:56.090
<i>They say it looked like 
a shiny black pearl.</i>

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:57.740
Wow!

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:00.560
Tell me how to make it!

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.360
Please.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.390
Okay.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:07.650
Let's all make them!

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:10.070
Yay!

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:13.520
That's the power of Tsunehisa-sama.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:15.160
You, too, Shimizu-kun!

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.370
They're all shiny!

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:20.670
Wow!

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.080
So shiny.

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:25.000
Tsunehisa-chan showed me how.

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:29.630
Who cares about mudballs?

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:33.140
<i>Tsunehisa had captured</i>

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:35.760
<b>Matsuda</b>

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:45.770
Slide 
Mountain

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:45.770
Faucet 
River

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:45.770
<b>Enya</b>

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:45.770
<b>Misawa</b>

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:35.980
<i>the people's hearts with her mudballs.</i>

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:45.770
<b>Amago</b>

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:39.990
<i>But the quick growth of her 
group brought friction.</i>

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:43.140
<i>Tensions with the Enya-kun group grew,</i>

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:45.770
<i>and a clash was imminent.</i>

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:47.800
<i>Tsunehisa decided to</i>

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.790
<i>overcome this with diplomacy.</i>

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:53.480
Enya-kun!

00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:57.800
You want something?

00:07:57.800 --> 00:07:59.790
Want to make a castle with everybody?

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:02.700
A castle?

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:06.220
My dream is to make a castle 
out of the whole sandbox!

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:10.750
But I don't see what I would get out of it.

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:11.750
Why?

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:15.990
With your people and our
ability to make those mudballs,

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:18.450
we can make a great castle.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:21.420
Even if we do, you're going 
to take the lead right?

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:23.850
Do you not like that?

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:25.510
That's not it.

00:08:25.510 --> 00:08:27.610
Then there's no reason to refuse.

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:30.900
It'll be fun. Let's do it together!

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:39.220
Your mudballs are so stupid!

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:43.660
You broke our mudballs!

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:46.290
You jerk!

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.370
Get them!

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:52.840
<i>This was the beginning of 
the famed mudball war.</i>

00:08:52.840 --> 00:09:02.670
Swingset Peak        Sand Plains

00:08:52.840 --> 00:09:02.670
<b>Enya</b>

00:08:52.840 --> 00:09:02.670
<b>Amago</b>

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:55.570
<i>Newly discovered records 
indicate that the</i>

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:58.790
<i>Tsunehisa and Matsuda-kun 
group forces numbered 60,000</i>

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:01.090
<i>while the Enya-kun group forces 
numbered 120,000.</i>

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:04.830
<i>The Matsuda-kun group was at 
a clear disadvantage,</i>

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:08.690
<i>and immediately, the battle 
lines began to collapse.</i>

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:12.360
No!

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:16.900
You jerk! You jerk!

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:21.330
<i>It was Tsunehisa who overcame 
this disadvantage.</i>

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:23.180
Shimizu-kun.

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:24.410
Turn on the faucet.

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:33.660
Get back!

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.800
<i>Undine's Razor,</i>

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:44.020
<i>as this super weapon would 
later come to be known,</i>

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.170
<i>was only made possible 
by the trust between</i>

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:47.850
<i>Shimizu-kun and Tsunehisa.</i>

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:53.820
<i>It also shows Tsunehisa's wisdom 
in first acquiring the water.</i>

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:57.410
<i>The introduction of this 
super weapon caused a quick rout</i>

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:59.320
<i>of the Enya-kun group forces.</i>

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:21.830
<i>It is said that Shimizu-kun</i>

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:25.440
<i>never forgot the beauty of the
rainbow that appeared then.</i>

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:29.280
<i>Tsunehisa had defeated Enya-kun,</i>

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:33.600
<i>but she refused to rule by force.</i>

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.940
Once we put water on it, we harden the

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:38.610
base as much as we can.

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:42.200
If it caves in, we just put more
sand on top to harden it.

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:46.300
Dig tunnels slightly downwards 
and they won't collapse.

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:47.790
You're right.

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:49.960
The tunnel's so long and 
it isn't collapsing.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:53.800
Harden the base and you can 
do all kinds of things.

00:10:57.530 --> 00:11:01.410
<i>Through sharing her 
architectural technology,</i>

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:03.850
<i>Tsunehisa succeeded in 
winning Enya-kun's trust.</i>

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:11.310
<b>Enya</b>

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:11.310
<b>Amago</b>

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:17.860
Slide 
Mountain

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:17.860
Faucet 
River

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:17.860
<b>Misawa</b>

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:08.150
<i>Having shown her talents as a ruler,</i>

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:11.510
<i>Tsunehisa had grown close to conquering 
the sandbox in a short time.</i>

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:17.860
<b>Amago</b>

00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:13.810
<i>But it was too fast.</i>

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:17.860
<i>And growth that's too fast 
invites swift retaliation.</i>

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:21.550
I have no choice but to fight.

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:23.620
No matter what I have to do.

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:30.210
Misawa-chan, what's wrong?

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:33.800
<i>Later, researchers would be divided</i>

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:37.210
<i>in judging Misawa-chan's actions here.</i>

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:40.020
<i>But what can be said for certain</i>

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:41.460
<i>is that it was a</i>

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:43.720
<i>complete betrayal of child society.</i>

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:46.930
Were you the one who sprayed Enya-kun

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:48.470
and his friends with water?

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:52.870
Well, Tsunehisa-chan?

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:53.690
Yes.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:55.980
Why did you do that?

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:59.330
And is it true you took the sprayer that

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:02.000
the teachers use to water the flowers?

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.250
I wanted to stop the fighting.

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:06.990
But you can't spray them with water.

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:12.570
<i>If Shimizu-kun had been here, 
he would have defended her.</i>

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:15.670
<i>But he wasn't.</i>

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:19.670
You're not allowed to play 
in the sandbox anymore, then.

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:28.870
<i>A cruel punishment that would later come</i>

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:32.180
<i>to be known as 
"Summer's Imprisonment."</i>

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:34.690
<i>Tsunehisa thought to herself,</i>

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:37.690
<i>"If only Shimizu-kun were alive."</i>

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:41.860
<b>Announcement: 
Shimizu-kun 
is out 
with a cold.</b>

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:41.860
<i>But her punishment was 
just for that one Friday.</i>

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:46.140
<i>The following Monday, 
Tsunehisa would be free,</i>

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:48.630
<i>but the effect this 
Friday had on history</i>

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:50.870
<i>cannot be understated.</i>

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:04.090
<i>On this day, negotiations were held</i>

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:05.880
<i>between Tsunehisa and Misawa-chan.</i>

00:13:06.940 --> 00:13:10.430
Let's play rock, paper, scissors to split up turns in the sandbox.

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:12.890
Taking turns is fine,

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:14.880
but can we do it for 
three days at a time?

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:16.480
Three days?

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:18.080
Yes. Three days.

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:21.410
I need three days to make a sandcastle.

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:24.780
But then I don't get to play 
in the sandbox for three days.

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:27.330
But I want to make a sandcastle

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:29.110
that uses the whole sandbox.

00:13:29.110 --> 00:13:30.280
It'll take three days.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:31.710
Two days at best.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:35.340
Otherwise, my subordinates 
would look down on me.

00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:38.670
The sandbox is the best part 
of playing at the day care.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:41.170
You're right.

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:43.530
On the slide and jungle gym,

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:46.180
you just slide and 
climb and spin around.

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:49.610
The sandbox is the only place
where you can use your imagination.

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:50.720
That's right.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:53.000
It's the only place you 
can use your imagination;

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:54.780
that's why I like it.

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:58.650
If you understand that, 
I think you can work with us.

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:00.350
Making this castle will 
be the biggest thing

00:14:00.350 --> 00:14:01.550
ever done in the sandbox.

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:03.080
I'm sure it will.

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:04.720
Then let's do it together.

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:06.110
If you can do it with us,

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:09.240
we won't even need to take 
turns using the sandbox.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:13.200
I refuse to call everyone doing 
the same thing creativity.

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:16.080
The only one being creative is you.

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:19.400
No. It's everyone being creative.

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:23.890
If everyone's being creative, we 
should take turns every day.

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:27.440
Isn't it better to have 
lots of little castles?

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:29.550
It needs to be big.

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:33.260
There's no point in further discussion.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.860
<i>Misawa-chan was correct.</i>

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:39.760
<i>Negotiations continued, 
but were fruitless.</i>

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:42.790
<i>Things needed to be 
settled another way.</i>

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:45.840
<i>But many feel that the 
battle that followed</i>

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:48.420
<i>was the finest example of Tsunehisa's</i>

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:50.280
<i>flexibility and creativity.</i>

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:53.450
Then let's decide by 
knocking down sticks.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:54.710
Sticks?

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:56.130
We'll each make a sand mountain,

00:14:56.130 --> 00:14:58.270
put a stick on top, 
and then take away

00:14:58.270 --> 00:14:59.980
sand without making it fall over.

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:01.490
Oh, "avalanche."

00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:02.940
Knocking-down-sticks.

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:05.810
The winner gets to use the 
sandbox for three days.

00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:07.570
Very well.

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:11.090
The battle will be tomorrow.

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:13.100
<b>Don't try this at home, kids!</b>

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:15.100
Let's practice knocking-down-sticks!

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:16.680
Yay! Avalanche!

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.630
Avalanche!

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:20.190
It's knocking-down-sticks, I said.

00:15:20.590 --> 00:15:22.110
Tsunehisa-sama.

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:23.730
It's okay, Shimizu-kun.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:27.400
I'm going to win, no matter what.

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:30.340
<i>And the day finally came.</i>

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:32.310
<i>The fated day.</i>

00:15:32.310 --> 00:15:33.630
<i>The sky clouded over,</i>

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:35.910
<i>and they say there were strong 
gusts of wind at times.</i>

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:43.500
It's finally time to settle this.

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:45.750
Indeed.

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:51.510
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:53.180
Yahoo!

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:55.080
I go first.

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:57.060
You may choose the stick.

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.920
<i>In a sport where two people take turns,</i>

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:02.520
<i>the one to go first usually 
has the advantage.</i>

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:05.530
<i>In the knocking-down-sticks competition between Tsunehisa and Misawa-chan,</i>

00:16:05.870 --> 00:16:08.650
<i>the second to go was allowed 
to choose the stick,</i>

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:10.070
<i>to make it fair.</i>

00:16:10.510 --> 00:16:13.410
<i>When Tsunehisa chose her stick 
and put it on the mountain,</i>

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:16.080
<i>she was able to touch the sand 
and feel how hard it was.</i>

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:22.210
<i>As she went second,
she knew this, unlike Misawa-chan.</i>

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:26.260
<i>And only Tsunehisa knew 
precisely how deep</i>

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:27.620
<i>she had put it in.</i>

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:30.050
<i>Misawa-chan was forced to compare</i>

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:31.700
<i>the lengths of the stick she remembered</i>

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:34.410
<i>and the stick sticking 
out of the sand,</i>

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:37.010
<i>and guess at how much was underground.</i>

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:39.770
<i>But then a question arose.</i>

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:43.130
<i>Why had Tsunehisa chosen 
a stick with leaves,</i>

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:44.980
<i>that acted as a guide to indicate 
how much was underground?</i>

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:47.190
Misawa-chan, you can start.

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:49.180
<i>Misawa-chan's first strike should be</i>

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:51.940
<i>one to learn the hardness 
of the sand mountain.</i>

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:53.810
<i>Everyone thought there 
would be no major</i>

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:55.710
<i>movements in the first 
part of the match.</i>

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:02.040
Tsunehisa-chan is done for.

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:06.680
She took a big chunk out of it!

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:08.380
<i>The instant she touched 
the sand mountain,</i>

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:09.890
<i>Misawa-chan judged its</i>

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:12.330
<i>hardness and how likely 
it was to collapse.</i>

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:14.590
This is the result of my practice.

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:18.350
<i>The situation became instantly tense.</i>

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:22.100
<i>This move had given 
Misawa-chan the clear advantage.</i>

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:44.830
Now you can't take any more sand.

00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:47.330
I don't think it will fall over yet.

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:51.440
Go on, it's your turn.

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:52.780
I know.

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:54.750
Then go on and take some sand.

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:57.320
Or will you admit defeat?

00:17:57.320 --> 00:17:59.390
I know, but give me a little more time.

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:00.970
You've lost.

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:03.260
Go on and admit it.

00:18:05.690 --> 00:18:07.850
It's nap time.

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:10.310
Come inside!

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:11.590
Right!

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:15.240
<i>Nap time was an absolute.</i>

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:17.920
<i>It was the rule of the day care.</i>

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:20.740
<i>That was Tsunehisa's plan.</i>

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:22.200
That's not fair!

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.340
Indeed.

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:27.460
But you were the first 
one to use the teacher.

00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:32.540
You were the last one to 
go before we took a break.

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:36.060
We can finish after nap time, okay?

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:39.150
<i>Tsunehisa had chosen the leafy branch</i>

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:41.800
<i>because it was more 
affected by the wind,</i>

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:44.810
<i>and had a high center of gravity, 
which made it unstable.</i>

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:46.940
Come on, Misawa-chan.

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:48.810
You need to nap.

00:18:49.340 --> 00:18:51.840
<i>But it wasn't certain that the stick</i>

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:53.840
<i>would fall down during nap time.</i>

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:58.260
<i>If the stick hadn't fallen 
by the end of nap time,</i>

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:00.580
<i>Tsunehisa would find it difficult to win.</i>

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:03.030
<i>And any more stalling 
would invite children,</i>

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:07.290
<i>other than Misawa-chan, 
to say she wasn't being fair.</i>

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:10.670
<i>The battle wasn't over yet.</i>

00:19:28.760 --> 00:19:30.580
Tsunehisa-sama wins.

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:31.520
Tsunehisa-sama!

00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:33.050
Yeah.

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:41.820
<b>Misawa</b>

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:41.820
<b>Amago</b>

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:44.120
Slide 
Mountain

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:44.120
Faucet 
River

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:41.920
<i>It was this that caused 
Tsunehisa to be known</i>

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:44.120
<b>Amago</b>

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:44.400
<i>as one of the greatest 
strategists of all time.</i>

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:46.950
<i>Sticks blow over easily in the wind.</i>

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:49.080
<i>If the battle is not settled quickly,</i>

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:52.540
<i>the wind will usually knock them down.</i>

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:56.640
Okay, everyone, let's do our best!

00:19:56.640 --> 00:19:57.920
Let's do our best!

00:19:57.920 --> 00:19:59.420
<b>Blueprint</b>

00:19:57.920 --> 00:19:59.420
<b>Authorized Personnel</b>

00:19:57.920 --> 00:19:59.420
<b>Only</b>

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:08.770
<i>The castle-making proceeded well.</i>

00:20:11.970 --> 00:20:18.000
<i>The design showcased Tsunehisa's 
talents as a castle builder.</i>

00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:21.280
Okay, turn the water on.

00:20:29.090 --> 00:20:31.890
Tsunehisa-sama, you did it!

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:33.150
I did it.

00:20:33.150 --> 00:20:35.380
But we all made this castle together.

00:20:36.180 --> 00:20:39.180
<i>They say the completed 
castle was so beautiful</i>

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:41.380
<i>that the children could not look away.</i>

00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:45.540
Okay, Tsunehisa-sama, 
finish it with this.

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:49.290
I saved this apple from snack time!

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:54.650
I call it Apple Castle!

00:20:54.970 --> 00:21:02.110
Hooray! Hooray!

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:59.750
<i>At this moment, Apple 
Castle was complete.</i>

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:02.110
<i>But then...</i>

00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:06.260
Warring States General Amago Tsunehisa!

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:07.990
Your secret treasure is mine!

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:12.910
Tsunehisa, prepare yourself!

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:20.670
The weird girl knocked it down!

00:21:21.610 --> 00:21:23.040
What are you crying for?

00:21:23.040 --> 00:21:24.710
You're a warring states general, right?

00:21:24.710 --> 00:21:25.800
Where's your secret treasure?

00:21:27.070 --> 00:21:29.100
H-Hold on a sec.

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:31.990
Get out of here, stupid!

00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:34.140
Die! Get lost!

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:38.200
Get lost! Get lost!

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:40.450
Hey! Don't cry!

00:21:41.280 --> 00:21:46.700
Get lost! Get lost!

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:46.700
What is wrong with you?!

00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:50.460
Wh-Who are you?

00:21:51.750 --> 00:21:53.790
Damn it, I'll get you!

00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:57.150
It's a pervert!

00:21:57.150 --> 00:21:58.790
Somebody catch her!

00:21:59.320 --> 00:22:01.450
<i>War is a futile and empty thing.</i>

00:22:01.450 --> 00:22:04.320
<i>Like a castle made of sand...</i>

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:07.970
<i>Perhaps only the grains 
of sand in the sandbox</i>

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:11.930
<i>know what happened here.</i>

00:23:45.740 --> 00:23:48.730
Next is Tokugawa Ieyasu, 
the Peaceful Empress.

00:23:49.280 --> 00:23:51.870
Next time on Sengoku Collection:

00:23:51.870 --> 00:23:54.280
"Peaceful Empress Extra."

00:23:54.750 --> 00:23:56.600
They say that Tsunehisa

00:23:56.600 --> 00:23:59.850
didn't think it was fair that 
she gets two episodes.
